{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"coexistent-unclear-icefish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nGerrit 3506 patch set 2 (3df64d38e14, a change that only edits tests/_isolation.py, the isolation-guard tests and a Windows deselect list) got Verified -1 from CI run 44911300869, job 136870796494 (`pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)`). 3 unrelated tests errored at the same second (2026-11-21T14:26:12Z) with `Failed: New entries appeared in REPO_ROOT during this test: ['.rebar/gate_runs']`:\n- tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py::test_completion_verdict_pins_to_schema\n- tests/scripts/test_observability_journal_bounding_1205.py::test_steady_state_run_does_not_read_a_whole_copy_of_the_journal\n- tests/unit/test_web_tool_gating.py::test_pass1_chunk_threads_web_from_criterion_routing\nSo some other test, on another xdist worker, created `<checkout>/.rebar/gate_runs` during that window. The leak did not appear in the 11 other Test Suite and Gerrit Verified Gate runs of Nov 21 that I checked.\n\n`.rebar/gate_runs` is written only by `rebar.llm.gate_runs` (`record_gate_run`, `hold_owner_lock`, `_materialize_stale_running`) and `rebar.llm.workflow.runs`, under `_repo_root(repo_root)`, which falls back to `config.repo_root()` (the checkout) when the caller passes no `repo_root`.\n\nLocally (macOS, origin/main + 3506), the 15 test modules that reference gate_runs, `*_start(`, `hold_owner_lock` or `record_gate_run` pass (533 passed) and leave no `.rebar/gate_runs` behind.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- A test reaches a gate-run writer with `repo_root=None` while its `config.repo_root()` resolves to the checkout, for example a status poll that materializes a stale running record, and only on some interleavings.\n- A detached gate daemon started by an earlier test finishes after that test's sandbox was torn down and writes its terminal record against the checkout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The writer is identified by a deterministic reproduction (for example a guard that fails the first test creating `<checkout>/.rebar/gate_runs`), recorded here.\n- [ ] The writer is pinned to its test's root, with a regression test, and the leak no longer reaches the checkout.","id":"e6f5-f793-67a1-443b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A test writes .rebar/gate_runs into the checkout under CI, erroring 3 unrelated tests through the repo-leak guard"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795277074350330001,"uuid":"ed4bb4c3-36a1-4794-8516-a3fd3137ce54"}